# Vault recycle publication plan

This plan proposes installation of the independently accepted finite entry-recycle slice and its exact two client guards. Production is unchanged. It executes no candidate, original program, browser, behavioral test or benchmark. Root owns installation, current verification, requirements metadata and publication.

`selected-file-map.final.json` is the authoritative source/path/hash map. `documentation-map.json` binds three proposed live documents, and `requirements-binding.json` binds the current requirements epoch while checking the unchanged original 159 source fingerprints and 232 capability IDs. `production-reference-baseline.json` identifies all31 current app source/test/doc files plus the selected historical41 receipt. These are proposal/reference records, not new implementation evidence.

## Installation boundary

Authenticate the current production source hashes before copying. Preserve the prior source bytes and current-history41/24-original-load receipt unchanged as a historical epoch. Install the exact final client, server and KDBX sources from the208-artifact correction stage; add its recycle module. History and XML stay exact. The KDBX change from current production is the single default `RecycleBinEnabled` value False→True in newDocument; existing imported native settings are honored. The final client differs from the original recycle546 client only in two post-active-list refresh checks: viewCurrent→binCurrent. Do not generalize those two fixes to untested browser boundaries.

Add the original recycle five test files and two oracle helpers. Three proposed path adapters are provided: recycle-harness.mjs defaults to the repository-local authenticated original assembly (REA_KEEPASS_EXE still overrides); its detailed output root changes to Studio .local; recycle-original.test.mjs and recycle-http.test.mjs likewise use Studio .local. Assertions and released helper behavior stay exact. The existing http-runner.mjs is already production-correct and byte-identical; retain it. The PowerShell oracle remains exact and test-only. Never install vendor executables or archive carriers as application runtime dependencies.

Four proposed independent adapters add the common boundary fixture, unchanged five boundary bodies, two independent confirmation controls and four author correction controls. The fixture's imports become app-local and its observations go to Studio .local. Test/helper bodies otherwise stay exact; proposed bytes are explicitly hashed in the map. No proposed adapter was executed in this plan.

Apply proposed-docs/README.md only against its recorded current README hash, and add RECYCLE.md/RECYCLE-NOTICE.md. The README retains its history evidence paragraphs—including12 local source ZIP carriers in the previous history epoch—while removing only entry recovery from the remaining-gap phrase and appending the finite recycle description. Documentation links are production-relative proposals which resolve after the mapped public payload is installed. Historic vendor Markdown/JS files remain inert .snapshot bytes.

## Evidence preservation without recursive recopying

Authenticate all four exact source inventories and their original manifests/freeze files:546 author,61 initial independent,208 correction,35 final independent. Map858 path records (850 manifest entries plus8 manifest/freeze objects) to471 unique public byte objects. Reuse27 already-public history snapshots after byte authentication; copy444 new unique inert blobs. The map records every original path and source identity, so overlapping run/source versions are not recursively recopied into nested history trees. Preserve original manifest bytes rather than rewriting them into a current manifest.

Keep the one1911-byte owned synthetic KDBX carrier local (SHA256 c79b1d0ea208df44fa0f137eb0ea9c5d0239212a58474834d11d63ea0d7f4d77). Record its exact path/bytes/digest as an explicit exclusion. The857 publishable path records still include all failed source versions, collectors, raw stdout/stderr, observations and negative diagnoses. The preservation manifest must distinguish original strict inventories from the reduced public byte set; it must not assert that all546 are public or invent a successful reconstruction of the excluded binary fixture.

The public payload must retain full selected source/license files, complete test/helpers for failed and accepted versions, every receipt/source manifest/freeze object, original default4.0 loss and conditional4.1 observations, source-composed clock adaptations, original failed-load counter correction, stale publication failure/control traces, invalid stale-token diagnosis and interruption records, and private-browser screenshots/accessibility observations. `selected-file-map.final.json` enumerates these rather than allowing a favorable-only selection. No original EXE/DLL/source ZIP is present in these four selected inventories. Other historical history-epoch carrier exclusions remain separately recorded.

The finite scan found no native header in selected public bytes and no quoted-base64 native carrier or exact original EXE/source ZIP digest. It found one native KDBX header, excluded above. Credential-like JSON values are tied to synthetic test/helper literals, with0 unresolved classifications. Exact raw records do contain local Windows username/path metadata (226 unique byte objects), and selected released source contains its copyright contact email. Preserve that privacy caveat; do not describe the payload as free of all personal data or all possible secrets. No user credential files were selected.

